# promise: #870
# ⌘W again and again on Favorites goes back through the ones visited before, newest first, as in Arc: F1, F2, F3 opened
# in turn, then ⌘W three times shows F2, F1, then nothing. 0.1.58 went F3 → F2 → F3: a Favorite closed with ⌘W keeps
# its page (#740), so it still counted as the tab shown before. CloseSuccessor.afterDeselectedFavorite walks
# SidebarStore's per-window ShownTabs and skips Favorites closed with ⌘W (favoritesClosedWithCmdW, as ⌃Tab does, #784).
budget rss=900 stalls50=20
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true}
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=fav1
expect-log n=fav1 HTTP
wait 1
cra://action/favoriteTab
wait 1
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=fav2
expect-log n=fav2 HTTP
wait 1
cra://action/favoriteTab
wait 1
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=fav3
expect-log n=fav3 HTTP
wait 1
cra://action/favoriteTab
wait 1
cra://debug?selectedTab=start
expect-log selected tab start: \S+n=fav3$
cra://action/closeTab
expect-log close tab: favorite deselected, its page kept
wait 1
cra://debug?selectedTab=first
expect-log selected tab first: \S+n=fav2$
cra://action/closeTab
wait 1
cra://debug?selectedTab=second
expect-log selected tab second: \S+n=fav1$
reject-log selected tab second: \S+n=fav3$
cra://action/closeTab
wait 1
cra://debug?selectedTab=third
expect-log selected tab third: none$
